---
description: Keep popup, options, and form UI from shifting when state or copy changes.
globs: **/*.css, **/*.tsx
alwaysApply: false
---

# Layout stability

Extension surfaces (popup, options, any future page) resize to content. Treat
conditional size changes as layout shift: helper text, validation, empty
states, badges, toasts, and expanding inputs.

Keep geometry stable across states:

- Reserve space for status, errors, and optional chrome (`min-height` / `min-width`)
- Overlay chips, tooltips, and explanations; do not insert a new row
- Swap copy in place; do not mount or unmount siblings that own layout
- Size inputs and controls for their longest valid value, suffix, or placeholder

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — error/help appears and the page grows
{error ? <p>{error}</p> : null}

// ✅ GOOD — reserved slot or overlay; neighbors do not move
<p className="field-status">{error ?? '\u00a0'}</p>
```

```css
.field-status {
  min-height: 1.35em;
}
```

Put extra copy in a reserved slot, an overlay, or `aria` text — not a new block
under the control.
